atlas provider

architecture placement-plane
  owns PlacementDemand
  owns PlacementReceipt
  consumes OperationIR
  consumes ProjectionIR
  consumes ProgramIR
  consumes Authority
  consumes FactDelta
  publishes PlacementPlan
  publishes PlacementReceipt
  canonical_name PlacementPlane
  family provider
  domain Provider / Runtime Placement
  layer provider/realization
  semantic_question Where may this realization execute, persist, project, and be delivered without changing who semantically owns it?
  purpose Compiles one provider-neutral PlacementDemand into Cloudflare delivery/material/coordination declarations, Supabase continuity projections, and Oracle native execution bindings. It makes every public control route, durable projection and recovery boundary reviewable from one declaration instead of coupling them through an incidental hostname or one provider's request path.
  maturity implemented
  node_types PlacementDemand
  node_types PlacementPlan
  node_types PlacementReceipt
  node_types FailureMatrix
  node_types ContinuityProjection
  edge_types places_on
  edge_types projects_to
  edge_types delivers_through
  edge_types reconstructs_from
  internal_calculus OperationIR / ProjectionIR / ProgramIR -> typed authority, mutability, latency, durability, visibility, mode, effect, data-gravity, failure-tolerance and cost demands -> three-provider realization plan -> evidence-bound PlacementReceipt
  internal_calculus compiler emits Cloudflare no-Worker exclusions before a broad estate route, ordered Tunnel ingress, direct R2 material-domain plan, Oracle gateway public origins, Supabase continuity schema, Oracle bindings and a per-provider failure matrix from schemas/control/placement-plane.cue
  internal_calculus full static export emits filesystem-visible route.html objects, then the R2 material publisher mirrors every emitted HTML route to its extensionless object key; this is a route-compatibility projection for direct material delivery, not a second page compiler. The estate Worker remains the public apex realization because it resolves a territory composition and host-specific material before selecting an R2 object
  internal_calculus OAuth authorization code exchange stores only a sealed session envelope in the Supabase continuity membrane and consumes it atomically; signing keys remain at the credential boundary and authority remains at BonfyreAuth
  internal_calculus public member paths that arrive through a broad static Worker preserve path/query and redirect to the territory's exact native session sibling; each sibling has an exact no-Worker route, a proxied Tunnel CNAME and ordered Tunnel ingress to WebAddress. When the free Worker request budget is exhausted, the four exact territory apexes can independently lower to the same native/Tunnel realization while wildcard subject delivery remains on the Worker. Authentication, account-link ownership and self-authoring remain native owners rather than Worker behavior
  invariant semantic authority != provider placement != durable projection != public delivery != execution
  invariant no realization may be the sole residence of truth required to reconstruct itself
  invariant a Cloudflare delivery object, Worker route, R2 body, Supabase row or Oracle process is replaceable residency and never semantic ownership
  invariant material.aurekai.work is a direct immutable R2 material lane and cannot silently become the human page-router, semantic owner, authority or proof boundary
  invariant a direct material lane cannot replace a territory apex Worker when the Worker resolves territory composition, host-specific subject material, search, or another public program
  invariant Supabase operational coordination state is a versioned projection; a stale projection cannot mint authority, complete an effect or supersede its native owner
  invariant an Oracle outage can stop advancement and native effects but cannot erase last proven public material, indexed projections, receipts or the declaration required to reconstruct execution
  invariant canonical MCP/Auth hosts and legacy aurekai.work compatibility paths explicitly bypass the broad static estate Worker; DNS pointing a canonical host at a Tunnel is insufficient while a wildcard Worker route still matches it
  invariant a route plan with a no-Worker exclusion is an ordered deployment instruction, not evidence that Cloudflare accepted it
  invariant a no-Worker member-session route is lawful only when its exact hostname has both a controlled Tunnel DNS binding and a matching Tunnel ingress; removing a Worker route from a territory apex alone sends the request to that apex's ordinary DNS origin, not to a native session owner
  forbidden_inference a provider selected -> semantic ownership or authority to execute
  forbidden_inference an available cheap provider -> a valid placement
  forbidden_inference a Supabase continuity row -> canonical fact or issuer authority
  forbidden_inference a PlacementReceipt planned -> route/tunnel/schema applied or healthy
  forbidden_inference a static public response -> Oracle is available or current truth has advanced
